# No Vercel infrastructure

This repo must stay **self-hostable and independent of Vercel’s platform**. Do not introduce or rely on Vercel-hosted services for core functionality.

## Forbidden (do not add or depend on)

- Vercel AI Gateway (`AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY`, string gateway model ids like `"anthropic/..."` as the production path)
- Vercel Connect (`@vercel/connect`, `connect()` for OAuth/MCP/OpenAPI)
- Vercel OIDC route auth (`vercelOidc()` as a required production authenticator)
- Vercel Sandbox (`vercel()` sandbox backend)
- Vercel-only deploy assumptions (Build Output API, Deployment Protection, project-linked OIDC) as the only supported path
- Requiring `vercel link` / Vercel CLI for the agent to work

## Required alternatives

| Need | Prefer |
| --- | --- |
| Models | Direct AI SDK providers or third-party gateways (e.g. Command Code) with env keys |
| Hosting | `eve build` + `eve start` (Nitro Node) or any non-Vercel host |
| Route auth | JWT, OIDC, Clerk, Auth.js, API keys, or custom `AuthFn` — not `vercelOidc()` |
| Connection OAuth | `defineInteractiveAuthorization` + your own token store, or static/user `getToken` |
| MCP / APIs | Remote MCP with self-hosted auth, OpenAPI connections, or authored tools |
| Sandbox | Local / Docker / microsandbox / custom backend — not Vercel Sandbox |
| Workflows | Local workflow world or self-hosted world packages |

## Scaffold cleanup

Do not reintroduce `eve init` Vercel defaults (`vercelOidc()`, `placeholderAuth()`, `@vercel/connect`, `.vercelignore`, gateway string models as the primary path).

## Review check

Before finishing work, confirm nothing new requires a Vercel account, Vercel project, or Vercel-hosted credential to run locally or in production.
